    "reading": "The instrument sets share no rsID. Exactly one cross-platform pair is in strong LD (rs191297708 UKB / rs79914289 deCODE, r2=0.705); all other 14 pairs are below r2=0.08. Critically, the STRONGEST instrument on each platform is nearly independent of everything on the other (deCODE rs10250602 F=715, max cross r2=0.074; UKB rs78840640 F=1405, max cross r2=0.011). So the two platforms' MR estimates are largely NOT instrumented by the same genetic variation. This is a concrete explanation for the discordance and does not require an epitope difference \u2014 but it is an observation about instrument selection, not proof, and it does NOT restore the pre-registered both-platform gate."
  },
  "verdict_combined": "Epitope/binding artifact NOT supported (0/8 instruments coding on either platform). The likelier explanation is that the platforms instrument different variation: no shared rsID, and each platform's strongest instrument is nearly independent of the other's. The UKB-PPP arm of the PDGFRB null REMAINS UNGATED and must stay disclosed."
